 - **Cards-checkout lifecycle tools** — `scripts/checkout-cards-close.ts` (official checkout2-0.js modal OR hosted page; `--no-close` supported) and reusable `scripts/close-transaction-verify.ts` (`closeOrReport`/`statusOf`/`closeAndVerify`, flags `--raw/--json/--status-only/--delay`) with the post-close interpretation table.
+- **Payment-link behavior controls** — `paymentLink.create` now documents and validates the behavior-driving params from the PayWay API: `paymentLimit` (omit = unlimited payments, `1` = single-use, `N` = multi-use up to N), `expiredDate` (`0`/omit = no expiry, epoch seconds = expires then), `currency` (min 0.01 USD / 100 KHR), and a new `payout` split-instruction array (each `{acc, amt}`; sum must equal amount). CLI `payment-link create` gains `--payout`, interprets `payment_limit`/`expired_date` into human-readable usage + validity lines, and `payment-link detail` now reports "X of N (remaining Y)" and "No expiry" vs absolute time. The `aba-payway-payment-link` skill documents every param, the callback `POST {tran_id,status,merchant_ref_no}` shape, and `PTL02/04/05/99/132` error codes.
+- **Payment-link payout wire-format fixes (per PayWay integration guidance)** — each beneficiary `amt` is now serialized as a **string** (`"5.00"`) inside the RSA-encrypted `merchant_auth`; `acc` is the ABA account/MID (numeric, not an API credential id); `payout` is omitted entirely when unused (never sent as `null`/empty). Added/forwarded `payout` through the agent `create_payment_link` tool and contract. Skill now lists payout gotchas and the `PTL-PAYOUT-36` (amount mismatch), `PTL146`/`PTL-PAYOUT-37`/`PTL46` (whitelist/type), `PTL-RSA-NOTFOUND`, and "Payout Info is invalid." errors.
