 The seven configuration fields can be supplied in the constructor (highest priority), environment (`PAYWAY_KHQR_BAKONG_ID`, `PAYWAY_KHQR_ABA_MERCHANT_ID`, `PAYWAY_KHQR_ACQUIRER_NAME`, `PAYWAY_KHQR_MERCHANT_CATEGORY_CODE`, `PAYWAY_KHQR_MERCHANT_NAME`, `PAYWAY_KHQR_MERCHANT_CITY`, and `PAYWAY_KHQR_PAYWAY_DATA`), or an optional local CLI profile. Keep them private and obtain them from ABA; do not infer or reuse another merchant's values.
 
+### Offline QR from the CLI
+
+```bash
+# Static QR for a table tent (no amount → reusable)
+payway-sdk generate-qr --offline --ref TABLE-7
+
+# Dynamic QR with amount, saved to payway-output/TABLE-7.png and self-verified
+payway-sdk generate-qr --offline --ref TABLE-8 -a 12.50 -c USD
+
+# Image flags work identically to online mode:
+#   --save-image <path> / --no-save-image / --open-image / --no-open-image
+```
+
+Offline mode renders the KHQR payload locally (no API image is available), saves it next to online QRs by default, and **self-verifies before printing**: the TLV is re-decoded, the CRC-16 checksum recomputed, and a summary (static/dynamic, amount, merchant name/city, Bakong ID, reference) shown so configuration mistakes surface immediately:
+
+```
+  ✓ Self-check passed (TLV decoded · CRC-16 CCITT valid)
+    Type:             Dynamic
+    Amount:           12.50 USD
+    Merchant:         Example Merchant — Phnom Penh
+    Bakong ID:        merchant@bakong
+    Reference:        TABLE-8
+```
+
+`payway-sdk doctor` reports the same readiness as an advisory row: fully unconfigured is fine (`optional`), but a **partial** configuration is flagged because every `--offline` run would fail until all 7 ABA fields are present.
+
 Omit `amount` for a static QR (`01=11`); provide it for a dynamic QR (`01=12` with tag `54`). The payload uses byte-aware TLV lengths, includes merchant reference `62.01`, ABA-provided PayWay data `62.68`, and CRC tag `63`. Earlier SDK versions used a private offline format; migrate by removing legacy `merchantId`, `transactionId`, tip, fee, and transaction-type arguments.
 
+Programmatic self-checks use the exported helpers:
+
+```typescript
+import { inspectKhqrPayload, validateKhqrCrc } from 'aba-payway-ts';
+
+const inspection = inspectKhqrPayload(qrString);
+if (!inspection?.valid) throw new Error('KHQR payload failed local verification');
+console.log(inspection.static ? 'Static QR' : `Dynamic ${inspection.amount} ${inspection.currency}`);
+```
+
 > ⚠️ **Important:** Offline-generated QRs cannot be tracked by PayWay for status. For server-side status tracking, use the API-based `generateQr()`. A payment notification, when ABA has provisioned one, still needs separate reconciliation.
 
